cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research preview, please cite it as below."
title: "Green Supplier Finance Lab"
abstract: >-
  A multi-country, multi-industry browser research preview. For a chosen buyer
  economy and industry it traces first-tier foreign supplier sectors from
  published OECD accounts (Inter-Country Input-Output 2025, 2022 table; GHG
  Footprints production-based emissions, 2022), allocates supplier-sector
  emissions and value added in proportion to the buyer's purchases, and lets the
  user test hypothetical decarbonisation-financing scenarios. Published accounts,
  modelled allocation and assumed financing are kept visibly distinct. It is not
  a firm-level carbon inventory, a credit assessment, a causal model or an
  investment recommendation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shukla
    given-names: Rahul
    roles: ["Concept", "Research design", "Interpretation"]
repository-code: "https://github.com/rahulsh97/rahulsh97.github.io"
url: "https://rahulsh97.github.io/green-supplier-finance-lab/"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-21"
keywords:
  - global value chains
  - green finance
  - input-output
  - production emissions
  - OECD ICIO
  - Scope 3 screening
references:
  - type: data
    title: "OECD Inter-Country Input-Output (ICIO) Tables, 2025 release, 2022 table"
    url: "https://www.oecd.org/en/data/datasets/inter-country-input-output-tables.html"
    notes: "Source of published intermediate-input, gross-output and value-added accounts. OECD is the source of the underlying accounts."
  - type: data
    title: "OECD Greenhouse Gas Footprints, production-based emissions (PROD_GHG), 2022"
    url: "https://www.oecd.org/en/data/datasets/greenhouse-gas-footprint-indicators.html"
    notes: "Source of production-based sector emissions."
notes: >-
  Engineering assistance: OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code. These tools
  provided software/engineering assistance and are not authors. OECD retains all
  rights in the underlying data; see NOTICE.md.
